Package: DOAS
Type: Package
Title: Double Observer Adjusted Survey Framework
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Achaz", "von Hardenberg", email = "achaz.hardenberg@unipv.it", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Estimates wildlife population abundance in gregarious and solitary
    species by combining standard block counts across survey sectors with
    double-observer (DO) surveys in a subset of sectors (or across all sectors).
    Supports both frequentist (Chapman and Zippin removal) and multi-chain
    Bayesian Markov Chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) estimators under independent and
    dependent double-observer protocols, with detection (p_formula) and abundance
    (n_formula) covariate modeling, S3 prediction, and simulation-based power analysis.
